17. BUILD AND RELEASE PLAN

Do not attempt the entire product in one code-generation step.

Build a sequence of complete, testable vertical slices.

Phase 0 — Repository and technical validation

Tasks:

- Inspect the repository and build configuration.
- Establish the target SDK and minimum supported version.
- Confirm compatible library versions.
- Define architecture boundaries.
- Create the design token system.
- Establish automated builds and tests.

Deliverable: A reproducible Android project that builds.

Phase 1 — Foundation

Implement:

- App navigation.
- LUMEN FLOW design system.
- Light, dark and high-contrast themes.
- Local persistence.
- Guest mode.
- Accessible shared controls.
- Error and loading states.

Deliverable: A functional shell with real navigation and local persistence.

Phase 2 — Calculator MVP

Implement:

- Basic arithmetic.
- Scientific functions.
- Expression editing.
- Angle modes.
- Calculation history.
- Domain errors.
- Precision policy.
- Automated mathematical tests.

Deliverable: A trustworthy offline calculator.

Do not proceed to advanced AI calculation claims until the underlying engine is verified.

Phase 3 — Verified learning

Implement:

- Structured derivations for supported problem types.
- Hint, outline and full solution modes.
- Unit-aware physics examples.
- Formula library.
- Topic and curriculum manifests.
- Student-working comparison for supported transformations.

Deliverable: A functioning calculation-and-understanding loop.

Phase 4 — First learning experience

Implement:

- Topic pages.
- Daily practice.
- Mistake journal.
- Revision scheduling.
- One complete mini-game.
- One validated simulation.

Deliverable: One coherent learning journey from explanation to practice.

Phase 5 — AI tutor

Implement:

- Contextual hints.
- Grounded explanations.
- Structured request parsing.
- Result validation.
- Optional online AI.
- Privacy disclosures.
- Graceful offline fallback.

Deliverable: An AI tutor that never replaces deterministic calculation verification.

Phase 6 — Expand the product

Add:

- More calculator modes.
- More games.
- Additional simulations.
- Graphing improvements.
- More validated curriculum content.
- Optional teacher tools.

Deliverable: A growing content library with consistent architecture.

Phase 7 — Accounts and synchronisation

Implement:

- Email registration.
- Verification.
- Password reset.
- Secure sessions.
- Progress synchronisation.
- Export and deletion.
- Conflict handling.

Deliverable: Optional account functionality without weakening guest access.

Phase 8 — Release readiness

Perform:

- Security review.
- Privacy review.
- Curriculum review.
- Accessibility testing.
- Mathematical regression testing.
- Device compatibility testing.
- Performance benchmarking.
- Release signing and store preparation.

Deliverable: A tested release candidate with a documented limitations list.

Phase 9 — Post-launch improvement

Use privacy-respecting feedback and validated product-health measurements to prioritise improvements.

Add content packs incrementally, monitor regressions and retain rollback capability.

Never make a feature mandatory merely to improve engagement metrics.

