20. MVP DEFINITION OF DONE

The first release candidate is not complete until all of the following are demonstrably functional.

Core experience

- Guest mode opens without registration.
- Basic and scientific calculations work offline.
- Expressions are editable.
- Errors are understandable.
- History persists locally.

Mathematical trust

- Supported equations have verified derivations.
- Numeric policies are documented.
- Reference tests pass.
- Invalid inputs are handled safely.
- AI does not bypass the calculation engine.

Learning

- At least one complete curriculum topic is available.
- Practice feedback explains mistakes.
- At least one revision workflow works.
- A student can save and resume progress.

Games and simulations

- At least one educational game is playable.
- At least one simulation has documented assumptions.
- Both work offline after installation.
- Wrong answers provide useful feedback.

Design

- All five primary navigation destinations work.
- Theme selection works.
- Accessibility basics are tested.
- Compact phone layouts are usable.
- No core screen consists only of mock data.

Privacy and reliability

- No advertisements.
- No student feature paywalls.
- No plaintext password storage.
- No unnecessary permissions.
- Local data survives normal navigation and process recreation.
- Failure states do not silently destroy work.

Delivery

- Project builds reproducibly.
- Automated tests run.
- Actual results are documented.
- Known limitations are disclosed.
- No claim is made that unimplemented features are complete.

